 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a pause before each retry that grows by 2
+seconds: 2, 4, 6, then 8 seconds, 20 seconds in all.
+
+The pauses exist because the gateway answers slowly every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00, its peak. Captures used to make
+3 attempts back to back within a second, so all three landed in the same slow minute: one Friday, 58 confirmed pantry
+orders were never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next
+morning. Replaying that Friday's timeouts against the gateway's sandbox, 5 attempts spaced this way would have
+captured 57 of the 58. Switching gateways was ruled out while the gateway's contract runs, to December 2026. The
+discussion is in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+## Known limits
+
+- A member whose capture times out waits on the confirmation page up to 20 seconds longer, through the pauses
+  between attempts. The team accepted the wait over volunteers capturing orders by hand.
+- A slow peak can outlast all 5 attempts: in the replay, 1 pantry order in 58 still gave up. Those orders stay
+  uncharged until someone follows [the gateway-timeouts runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md).
+
